@k.words.constantine.noun.1 k.words.sense word=Constantine pos=noun n=1 supersense=noun.person gloss="Emperor of Rome who stopped the persecution of Christians and in 324 made Christianity the official religion of the Roman Empire; in 330 he moved his capital from Rome to Byzantium and renamed it Constantinople (280-337)" synonym="Constantine I" synonym="Constantine the Great" synonym="Flavius Valerius Constantinus" instance_of="Roman Emperor" core.source="wordnet 3.1"
